@{
 
}

<h1> Player Application</h1>


<form method="post" asp-controller="PlayerApplication" asp-action= "Index">
    <input type="hidden" name="selectedSportName" value="@Model.SelectedSportName" />
    <input type="hidden" name="selectedRole" value="@Model.SelectedRole" required/>
    <div>
        <label for="FirstName">First Name</label>
        <input type="text" Name="FirstName" class="form-control" value="" required />
    </div>
    <div>
        <label for="LastName">Last Name</label>
        <input type="text" Name="LastName" class="form-control" value="" required/>
    </div>
    <div>
        <label for="DateOfBirth">Date Of Birth</label>
        <input type="date" Name="DateOfBirth" class="form-control" value="" required/>
    </div>
    <div>
        <label for="PreferredPosition">Preferred Position</label>
        <select name="PreferredPosition" class="form-control" id="PreferredPosition">
            <option value="">-- Select Positiion --</option>
            @if (@Model.Sports != null)
            {
                foreach (var pos in Model.Sports)
                {
                    <option value="@pos" selected="@(Model.PreferredPosition == pos ? "selected" : null)">@pos</option>
                }
            }
        </select>
    </div>

    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
</form>

        @* This code creates a web page for submitting a player application.
What it does:
•	Displays a welcome message.
•	Shows the selected sport and role from the model.
•	Contains a form for the user to enter:
•	First Name
•	Last Name
•	Date of Birth
•	Preferred Position (dropdown, options come from Model.Sports)
•	The dropdown for "Preferred Position" is filled with positions from the model, and the current preferred position is pre-selected if available.
•	Includes hidden fields to keep the selected sport and role values.
•	When the form is submitted, it sends the data to the Index action of the PlayerApplication controller.
In short:
This page lets users fill out and submit a player application, including their personal details, selected sport, role, and preferred position. *@